---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
List a run's property (assertion) results, one table per group.

Each property has its ID, name, group, and status: passing, failing, or
undetermined. An undetermined property has not triggered yet. Each property also
counts its examples and its counterexamples.

Each table is headed by its group; columns are STATUS, ✓, ✗, ID, NAME (failing
first). STATUS is pass, fail, or unseen, for undetermined. ✓ is the example
count and ✗ is the counterexample count; large counts are shortened, as in 186k.
ID is the property ID.

Filter by status with --passing, --failing, and --undetermined. Give more than
one to show each of those statuses.

Narrow with --name and/or --group. Both are case-insensitive substring matches
against the relevant fields. Add --detail to expand the matches into their
examples and counter-example moments instead of the table. Pass a moment to
`snouty runs logs <run_id> <input_hash> <vtime>` to read the logs leading up to
it. To show one property in full, pass its ID to
`snouty runs property <run_id> <property_id>`.

Examples:
  snouty runs properties <run_id> --failing
  snouty runs properties <run_id> --failing --undetermined
  snouty runs properties <run_id> --name eventually_validate --detail
  snouty runs properties <run_id> --group Unreachable --detail

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each property prints as one JSON object
on its own line. --json is mutually exclusive with --detail:
  snouty --json runs properties <run_id> --failing | jq -r .name

Usage: snouty runs properties [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --passing
          Show passing properties; combine with the other status filters

      --failing
          Show failing properties; combine with the other status filters

      --undetermined
          Show undetermined properties; combine with the other status filters

      --name <NAME>
          Filter properties by name (matched by substring, case-insensitive)

      --group <GROUP>
          Only properties whose group contains this substring (case-insensitive)

  -d, --detail
          Expand each matching property into its examples / counter-example
          moments, instead of the summary table

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
